The two words {{Lang|iry|bidu'}} and {{Lang|iry|umaning}} both translate to 'how much, how many' but have different uses. Examples of these question words are given below:

* {{Lang|iry|Bidu' mada dayu' ag gura'an?}} 'How far (how much distance) is it to town?'
* {{Lang|iry|Umaning aku kuyay kawu?}} 'How much older am I than you?'{{Citation needed|date=May 2019}}

The latter sentence uses {{Lang|iry|umaning}} because it is counting age.

